# Hourly eviction for the runner's host-bound cache/builds directories: 24h
# rule, `fuzz-corpus-*` exempt from it, 200 GiB cap on the cache as the
# backstop. The script header holds the whole contract.
#
# stdout and stderr go to /dev/null deliberately — the channel is syslog. The
# sweep logs every deletion and every refusal through `logger` (refusals at
# `user.err`), which is what survives dcron; duplicating it here would only
# fill root's mail spool with the same lines.
#
# Running hourly is safe against overrun: the sweep takes `flock -n` on
# /var/run/runner-cache-sweep.lock and exits 0 with `skipped: another sweep
# holds ...` if the previous run is still walking the trees, so two `rm -rf`
# passes can never overlap on the same directories.
#
# Invoked as `/bin/bash <path>` rather than executed: /boot is vfat and cannot
# carry an exec bit.
20 * * * * /bin/bash /boot/config/scripts/runner-cache-sweep.sh > /dev/null 2>&1
